  id: W4_04
  era: "1857\u20131858"
  title: Rani Lakshmibai of Jhansi
  text: Rani Lakshmibai of Jhansi. In 1857 Indian soldiers of the Company army rose in revolt at Meerut, and the uprising spread across northern India. The Rani of Jhansi became one of its most famous leaders; she died fighting near Gwalior in June 1858. After the revolt, the British Crown took over the government of India. Other leaders of 1857 included the last Mughal emperor Bahadur Shah Zafar, Nana Sahib, Tantia Tope, Kunwar Singh and Begum Hazrat Mahal of Awadh.
